<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gero the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900–965</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Margrave Gero</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gero the Great was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> noble whom Otto I appointed in 937 to command the eastern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>. He extended German rule over the Slavic lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> and Oder through harsh campaigns and in 963 forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-i">Mieszko I of Poland</a> to pay tribute. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gernrode-abbey">Gernrode Abbey</a>, and after his death in 965 his vast march was divided.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gero-the-great.jpg" alt="Gero the Great" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Mhf77 at German Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gero.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
